{"assets":["/editorial-assets/4d80afad9eb93e6a70b38a5e8047384fbcf74b80e7951c3d227981b95a935df7.png","/editorial-assets/0f082d5da73a917748dd0b47075405bfcc48a086ef0adbba0a7a1aa7e7ee0d37.png","/editorial-assets/fc44f748ff6360a7494070823b2a7b93d73d6f2574ae1e72043d3c9fde859d59.png","/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png","/editorial-assets/4237f553bf315cbc75f63dee3be515a20dce144717e1926cc4de7fef2470f7f8.png"],"contestId":"176","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A div2."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" Required row is row that have only one star inside. Requred column is comumn that also have only one star inside. So, you can iterate over all rows/columns, calculate number of stars inside them and find the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Authors are "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/MikeMirzayanov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MikeMirzayanov"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Gerald"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gerald"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" ."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B div2."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" Naive solution "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") (where you check all triplets) doesn't fin into time limits."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can see that for every two points from triplet (for example, for A and C) you can find place of the third point. So you can find number of requred triplets just inerate over all pairs of points and check middle point between points in every pair."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How to fast check position? You can add 1000 for all coordinates (you can see that this operation doesn't change the answer) and mark them in the 2-dimensional boolean array 2001х2001. So you can check every position for point in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1) time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Obtained solution works in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Authors are "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/MikeMirzayanov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MikeMirzayanov"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Gerald"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gerald"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A div1. C div2."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" In this problem some greedy solution expected."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let fix 2 planets: in planet i we will buy items, in planet j we will sell the ones. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Profit of item"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" of type k will be b_jk-a_ik. Every item has size 1, so you should greedy take items in order of decreasing of profits of items while you have place in the hold."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Scheme of full solution: you should iterate over all pairs of planet, for every pair greedy take items and find total profit. At the end you should find maximal total profit over all pairs and output it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Author is "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Ripatti"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ripatti"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B div1. D div2."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" You can see that split oparetion is just cyclically shift of string. You can go from any cyclically shift to any other one except the current one."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call some cyclically shift "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" iff it equal to the final string. All others cyclically shifts we will call "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bad"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". You can check all shifts in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") time. Let's you have A good shifts and B bad ones."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define dpA[n] as number of ways to get some good shift using n splits and за dpB[n] as number of ways to get some bad shift using n splits."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpA[0]=1, dpB[0]=0 or dpA[0]=0, dpB[0]=1 according to the first shift is good or not. All other values of dp you can get using following reccurences:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpA[n] = dpA[n-1] * (A-1) + dpB[n-1] * A"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpB[n] = dpA[n-1] * B + dpB[n-1] * (B-1)"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Answer will be dpA[k]. So you have "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") solution."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Also this problem can be solved in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/4d80afad9eb93e6a70b38a5e8047384fbcf74b80e7951c3d227981b95a935df7.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Author is "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/havaliza"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"havaliza"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C div1. E div2."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" The second player have easy strategy to hold some chip in position ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") in one of four half-planes — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 2, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 2, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 2 и "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 2. He can chose one of these half-planes by himself."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So, in case "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2|, |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2|) > 4 the second player wins — he just holds chips in half-planes that have no common cells."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Cases for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2|, |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2|) ≤ 4 expected to solve using some bruteforce. You can see that moving chips in way of distancing from each other is not profitable for the first player. Therefore you can bruteforce the game in square no more than 5 × 5. If your bruteforce so slow and doesn't fit into 2 sec, you can use precalculation. Also you can write some dp using masks."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Also you can check cases "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2|, |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2|) ≤ 4 by hand. But there you can easy make some mistakes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Author is "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Ripatti"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ripatti"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D div1."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" Let's define "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pre"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] as the minimal prefix of hyperstring that have with prefix of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" of length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" largest common sequence of length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then you have see reccurences:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pre"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"min"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pre"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"],  leftmost position of letter "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pre"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" that right than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pre"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1])."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For finding value of the second part inside min-function of formula above in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1), you should calculate some additional dp's: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp1 — for every basic string, positions inside of them and letter you should calculate leftmost position of current letter that right than current position;"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp2 — for every element of array of basic strings (it is hyperstring) and letter you should calculate leftmost basic string that have current letter and this string is rinht than current basic string."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So you have "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0f082d5da73a917748dd0b47075405bfcc48a086ef0adbba0a7a1aa7e7ee0d37.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" solution."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Author is "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/havaliza"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"havaliza"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E div1."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" At the first let's try to solve another problem: we have "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" chosed vertices in the tree and we want to find sum of subtree that \"spanned\" dy them in time "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/fc44f748ff6360a7494070823b2a7b93d73d6f2574ae1e72043d3c9fde859d59.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" (with any preprocessing time)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's sort all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices in order of dfs traversal — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", ... , "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". Consider pathes v1-v2, v2-v3, ... , v(k-1)-vk and vk-v1. You can see that they cover only our requred subtree and every edge is covered exactly two times. So you can just find sum of lengths of these pathes (you can do it in required "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/fc44f748ff6360a7494070823b2a7b93d73d6f2574ae1e72043d3c9fde859d59.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" time using LCA algo) and divide obtained value by 2."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For solving initial problem you should support set of active vertices in ordered state (for example, you can use std::set) and sum of all pathes between all neighbour vertices. Now you can process insert/remove queries in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", and recalculate sum of pathes by finding no more than 3 new pathes also in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So you have "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/4237f553bf315cbc75f63dee3be515a20dce144717e1926cc4de7fef2470f7f8.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" solution."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Author is "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Ripatti"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ripatti"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/4372"}